# Normalize all text files to LF in the repository and on checkout, regardless of
# a contributor's core.autocrlf setting. Without this, a Windows clone with
# autocrlf=true rewrites files to CRLF, producing whole-file diffs (and, for *.sh,
# bash failures: "$'\r': command not found"). text=auto lets git auto-detect and
# leave binary files untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt-and-suspenders for files that MUST stay LF to run in the Linux container.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
